  "id": "Compound::DB01151 - Gene::1562",
  "verbalization": "Desipramine, a tricyclic antidepressant, appears to interact with multiple cytochrome P450 enzymes through a shared mechanism of binding to arachidonic acid epoxygenase activity. This interaction is supported by three distinct paths, all of which indicate that Desipramine binds to Cyp2c18 via a common intermediate, Arachidonic Acid Epoxygenase Activity, which is also engaged by Cyp2e1 and Cyp2d6. The cumulative scores from these paths suggest a plausible, though not definitive, link between Desipramine and Cyp2c18, mediated through the epoxygenase pathway. The shared involvement of these enzymes in the same metabolic process implies that Desipramine may influence the activity of Cyp2c18, potentially affecting the metabolism of arachidonic acid and its derivatives. The mechanism is consistent with the observed binding and functional participation, but further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the direct relationship between Desipramine and Cyp2c18.",
